iMac 5K: accept the right tile's link when only interlane alignment is pending

Applies ON TOP of imac5k-lean-core-7.2.x.patch.

The right-tile (slave) DP link sometimes failed to come up on a modeset or
DPMS wake: "enabling link 1 failed: 15" (DC_FAIL_DP_LINK_TRAINING), in about
one boot in five and about one slave bring-up in 45 overall. The panel
looked normal afterwards, but each failed attempt costs a retrain and the
full failure leaves the link up only because the last attempt keeps the PHY
on.

Clock recovery and channel EQ succeed on every attempt. The failure is the
link-loss check in dp_transition_to_video_idle() (non-eDP links only, so the
root tile never runs it): 5 ms after the training pattern goes off, the
slave sink has cleared INTERLANE_ALIGN_DONE (DPCD 0x204) while every lane
still reports CR_DONE, CHANNEL_EQ_DONE and SYMBOL_LOCKED (0x202/0x203 =
0x77 0x77). Alignment does not come back within 150 ms of polling, and
retraining reproduces the same state; once video is running the sink sets
INTERLANE_ALIGN_DONE again by itself (0x204 = 0x81, then 0x01, on both
tiles).

So for the Apple tiled slave only, a link loss reported after video idle
is accepted when the re-read lane status shows CR, EQ and symbol lock on
every active lane. Any other lane-level loss still fails the attempt and
falls back as before, and every other link is untouched.

Tested on the iMac18,3 (linux-omarchy 7.2.15), 100 DPMS off/on cycles: the
check accepted an alignment-only loss in 52 of 99 slave bring-ups, with no
failed training attempt and no "enabling link failed". Before the fix,
attempt 1 failed in 7 of 8 bring-ups.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c
@@ -1524,6 +1524,37 @@
 
 }
 
+/*
+ * The Apple 5K second tile clears INTERLANE_ALIGN_DONE as soon as the
+ * training pattern goes off and sets it again only once video arrives,
+ * while clock recovery, EQ and symbol lock hold on every lane. Retraining
+ * cannot change that, so accept the link when alignment is all it lacks.
+ */
+static bool apple_5k_slave_lt_align_only(struct dc_link *link,
+					 const struct link_training_settings *lt_settings)
+{
+	uint8_t dpcd_buf[6] = {0};
+	union lane_status lane_status;
+	uint32_t lane;
+
+	if (!dc_link_is_apple_tiled_slave(link) ||
+	    core_link_read_dpcd(link, DP_SINK_COUNT, dpcd_buf,
+				sizeof(dpcd_buf)) != DC_OK)
+		return false;
+
+	for (lane = 0; lane < (uint32_t)lt_settings->link_settings.lane_count; lane++) {
+		lane_status.raw = dp_get_nibble_at_index(&dpcd_buf[2], lane);
+		if (!lane_status.bits.CHANNEL_EQ_DONE_0 ||
+		    !lane_status.bits.CR_DONE_0 ||
+		    !lane_status.bits.SYMBOL_LOCKED_0)
+			return false;
+	}
+
+	DC_LOG_HW_LINK_TRAINING("%s: link(%d) lanes locked, interlane align pending video\n",
+				__func__, link->link_index);
+	return true;
+}
+
 static enum link_training_result dp_transition_to_video_idle(
 	struct dc_link *link,
 	const struct link_resource *link_res,
@@ -1547,8 +1578,12 @@
 		 */
 		if (link->connector_signal != SIGNAL_TYPE_EDP && status == LINK_TRAINING_SUCCESS) {
 			msleep(5);
-			if (!link->skip_fallback_on_link_loss)
+			if (!link->skip_fallback_on_link_loss) {
 				status = dp_check_link_loss_status(link, lt_settings);
+				if (status == LINK_TRAINING_LINK_LOSS &&
+				    apple_5k_slave_lt_align_only(link, lt_settings))
+					status = LINK_TRAINING_SUCCESS;
+			}
 		}
 		return status;
 	}
